X:1
T:Hungarian Dance No. 4
C:Johannes Brahms
O:Hungarian Dance No. 4 in F-sharp minor
N:The first 16 bars of the theme; the repeat an octave higher reaches F#7 and is
N:left out. Transposed down a tritone from F-sharp minor to C minor, so the lowest
N:note is C4 and the highest E-flat 5. The long notes of the original ring on into
N:the next pickup; here the first bar starts with an eighth rest in their place,
N:so the tune loops on whole bars. The small grace notes before the second eighth
N:of each pickup are left out. Melody from the flutetunes.com MIDI. Chords derived
N:from the melody.
M:2/4
Q:1/4=63
L:1/8
K:Cm
